# 3. Critical Findings (P0 and P1)

### Finding 1: Unauthenticated Public Read/Write Access to Entire Cloud Workspace & Plaintext Staff Passwords
- **Classification:** Confirmed security vulnerability
- **Priority:** **P0 (Critical)**
- **File(s) and Function(s) Affected:**
  - [`firestore.rules`](file:///c:/Users/USER/Documents/fdrmnn/WAFFLEO%20POS/Waffleo-POS/firestore.rules#L16-L18) (`isOwnerOrSharedWorkspace`) and [`firestore.rules:188-244`](file:///c:/Users/USER/Documents/fdrmnn/WAFFLEO%20POS/Waffleo-POS/firestore.rules#L188-L244)
  - [`WaffleoRepository.kt`](file:///c:/Users/USER/Documents/fdrmnn/WAFFLEO%20POS/Waffleo-POS/app/src/main/java/com/example/data/repository/WaffleoRepository.kt#L195-L214) (`observeStaffAccounts`, `saveStaffAccount` at line 496)
  - [`WaffleoLocalStore.kt`](file:///c:/Users/USER/Documents/fdrmnn/WAFFLEO%20POS/Waffleo-POS/app/src/main/java/com/example/data/local/WaffleoLocalStore.kt#L559) (`saveStaffAccounts`)
  - [`firebase_applet_config.xml`](file:///c:/Users/USER/Documents/fdrmnn/WAFFLEO%20POS/Waffleo-POS/app/src/main/res/values/firebase_applet_config.xml#L3)
- **Root Cause:** `isOwnerOrSharedWorkspace(userId)` in `firestore.rules` returns `true` whenever `userId == 'waffleo_master_workspace'` without checking `isAuthenticated()` (`request.auth != null`). In addition, `staff_accounts` stores staff and owner passwords in unhashed plaintext in both Firestore and `SharedPreferences`.
- **How the Problem Occurs:** Any person who extracts `firestore_database_id` and project ID from the APK can query `/users/waffleo_master_workspace/staff_accounts` without authenticating, dump all Owner/Developer/Supervisor/Kasir passwords in plaintext, and modify or delete orders and financial records across all branches.
- **Business Impact:** Total compromise of financial data, staff credentials, and multi-branch operational integrity.
- **Recommended Solution:** Require `isAuthenticated()` (at minimum Firebase Anonymous Auth or per-branch Google Auth) in `isOwnerOrSharedWorkspace(userId)`, and store PBKDF2/BCrypt/SHA-256 salted password hashes instead of plaintext passwords in `StaffAccount`.
- **Verification Method:** Run `node --test firestore.test.js` and `WaffleoRepositoryRuleTest` against the Firestore Emulator asserting unauthenticated reads/writes to `users/waffleo_master_workspace` fail with `PERMISSION_DENIED`.

