  1. `deleteBranchCascadeInCloud` filtered catalog documents to delete using `doc.id.lowercase().contains(baseSlug)`. If a branch is named `"Choco"`, `"Waffle"`, `"Kopi"`, or `"A"`, `doc.id.lowercase().contains(baseSlug)` matches Global catalog items (`waffle_choco`, `waffle_polos`, etc.) and permanently deletes them from Firestore!
  2. `BranchProfile.displayName` and `WaffleoViewModel.getBranchDisplayName` hardcoded `"Gabek"` whenever `name.isBlank()` or `branchId.contains("-") && branchId.length > 20` (which matches every UUID `branch_<uuid>` generated by `createNewBranchByDeveloper`).
  3. `deleteBranchPermanently` adds the human-readable branch `name` (`resolvedName.lowercase()`, `baseSlug`) to `_deletedBranchIds`. If a new branch is later created with the same display name, `isBranchDeleted(branchName)` falsely flags the name as deleted.
- **How the Problem Occurs:** Developer creates a branch and later deletes it, or creates a new UUID branch whose profile name hasn't synced yet.
- **Business Impact:** Cross-branch catalog destruction in Firestore and mislabeling of new branches as `"Gabek"`.
- **Recommended Solution:** Remove `doc.id.lowercase().contains(baseSlug)` in `deleteBranchCascadeInCloud` (match strictly by `branchId` field or prefix when `branchId` is blank), and remove the hardcoded `"Gabek"` fallback for non-Gabek branch IDs.
- **Verification Method:** Unit test [`branchProfile_displayName_doesNotFallbackToGabekForNewUuidBranches`](file:///c:/Users/USER/Documents/fdrmnn/WAFFLEO%20POS/Waffleo-POS/app/src/test/java/com/example/ExampleUnitTest.kt#L783-L799) (executed and passed).

