### Finding 9: Single Global Document (`workspace_settings/global_config`) Overwrites Concurrent Multi-Branch Settings & Truncates `recappedOrderIds` at 500
- **Classification:** Architectural weakness & Confirmed bug
- **Priority:** **P1 (High)**
- **File(s) and Function(s) Affected:**
  - [`WaffleoViewModel.kt:5990-6250`](file:///c:/Users/USER/Documents/fdrmnn/WAFFLEO%20POS/Waffleo-POS/app/src/main/java/com/example/ui/viewmodel/WaffleoViewModel.kt#L5990-L6250) (`syncWorkspaceSettingsToCloud`, `applyCloudWorkspaceSettings`)
  - [`firestore.rules:180-186`](file:///c:/Users/USER/Documents/fdrmnn/WAFFLEO%20POS/Waffleo-POS/firestore.rules#L180-L186) (`isValidWorkspaceSettings`)
- **Root Cause:** All branches' `moneyBookmarks`, `bankAccounts`, `digitalWallets`, `customMenuCategories`, `customModifierCategories`, `deletedBranchIds`, and `recappedOrderIds` are serialized into one JSON string (`payloadJson`, capped at 50,000 chars by `firestore.rules:185`) inside `workspace_settings/global_config`. Furthermore, `recappedOrderIds` is truncated via `.take(500)` (`Set.take(500)` has arbitrary iteration order), and `applyCloudWorkspaceSettings` overwrites local `moneyAccounts` and `moneyCategories` whenever `cloudUpdatedAt > localUpdatedAt`.
- **How the Problem Occurs:** Two branches update settings or close store around the same time, or a workspace accumulates >500 recapped orders.
- **Business Impact:** Last-writer-wins data loss across branches, failure to save settings once `payloadJson` exceeds 50,000 characters, and arbitrary eviction of `recappedOrderIds`.
- **Recommended Solution:** Partition `workspace_settings` per branch (`workspace_settings/config_<branchId>`) and store `isRecapped` as a boolean field directly on `OrderRecord` rather than an unbounded ID array in `global_config`.
- **Verification Method:** Inspect `syncWorkspaceSettingsToCloud` payload growth and test multi-branch concurrent updates.

